<%# The same figure as the home page's hero, so the same treatment: .tw-card, the numeral doing the
    work, and design.md's icon tile rather than an illustration.

    It was bg-white with its own rounded-xl border and an h-[150px] fixed height, holding a 170px
    investment-funds.png pushed out of the box with inline `style="height: 170px; margin-bottom:
    -8px"`. Three arbitrary values to make a raster overflow a card whose height only existed to
    contain it. And it was the second illustration for one concept - the home page used a piggy bank
    for the same number.

    Illustration belongs in empty states and onboarding, not beside a live balance, which is where
    every finance app puts it. %>
<div class="tw-card p-5">
  <div class="flex items-start gap-4">
    <span class="grid size-9 shrink-0 place-items-center rounded-xl bg-emerald-50">
      <%= lucide_icon "piggy-bank", class: "size-5 text-emerald-700" %>
    </span>

    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">My earnings to invest</p>
      <p class="mt-1 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums">
        <%= number_to_currency(@portfolio.cash_balance) %>
      </p>

      <% if !current_user.student? %>
        <%# Was bg-slate-400 with slate-700 ink: 4.04:1, under the 4.5:1 gate for text, in a
            hand-rolled rounded-full pill. tw-btn-primary-disabled is the named token. %>
        <span aria-disabled="true" class="tw-btn-primary-disabled mt-3 w-fit">Invest now</span>
      <% elsif !current_page?(stocks_path) %>
        <%# No CTA when the card is already on the trading floor: it linked to stocks_path from
            stocks#index, so the page's one filled primary went nowhere. The balance is still worth
            showing there, which is why the card stays. %>
        <%= link_to "Invest now", stocks_path, class: "tw-btn-primary mt-3 w-fit" %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
